  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 974862,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1001 Logo: A Puzzle Collection for the Commodore 64\n\nStep into the provocative world of *1001 Logo*, a collection of three distinct puzzle games for the Commodore 64, punctuated by digitized female figures between levels. While the visuals might be unconventional, the gameplay offers a unique and challenging experience.\n\nThe core gameplay revolves around recreating patterns using stones, each with a numerical value that adds complexity. In the first game, you must replicate a displayed stone combination by strategically placing stones onto the playfield. Each placement alters the values of surrounding stones, demanding careful planning and foresight. Games two and three shift the focus to clearing pre-defined patterns. Game two involves clicking stones to remove them and adjacent stones, potentially creating new ones. Game three introduces a restriction: only two stones of the same color and value can be removed at once, adding a layer of tactical depth.  All moves in games one and three can be undone, offering a safety net for experimentation.  Can you conquer all 120 levels of each game?"
    },
